Power K is a liquid foliar fertilizer containing nitrogen (from urea) and potassium (from KOH), so it falls in heading 3105. Heading 3105 covers mineral or chemical fertilizers containing two or three of the fertilizing elements nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium. Subheading 3105.90 covers "other" such fertilizers, which is where a product with only N and K belongs. Heading 3105 includes packages of 10 kg or less, but this product is in 1-liter containers, so I considered 3105.10 (tablets or similar forms, or packages of gross weight not exceeding 10 kg). 3105.10 covers goods "in tablets or similar forms or in packages of a gross weight not exceeding 10 kg," so it applies here. Its statistical suffixes are 3105.10.00 with 10 digits: 3105.10.0000.

That said, the composition is partly potassium hydroxide, but the product is described and marketed as a fertilizer containing N and K. Because the 1-liter package is under 10 kg gross (1.36 kg), 3105.10.0000 is appropriate.

{"hts_code": "3105.10.0000", "reason": "A liquid N-K mineral/chemical fertilizer (urea plus potassium hydroxide) imported in 1-liter containers weighing under 10 kg gross falls under heading 3105, in the subheading for packages of 10 kg or less."}
